 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### routing — `/sc:workflow` is the default planner; `/task-builder` is for level 4 only
+
+#### Changed (default planner)
+
+- The routing guide (`HOW-WE-WORK.md`), its copy in core `CLAUDE.md`, and the plugin copy now make level 3 (`/sc:workflow` then `/sc:implement`) the default for any planned change with clear requirements, including work that touches many files or takes more than one session. Level 4 (`/task-builder` then `/task`) is now only for building a whole project or major component from scratch, from a spec complex enough that it nearly warrants a PRD and TDD.
+- Tie-break: "If you are unsure between levels 3 and 4, choose level 3. If you are unsure between any other two rows, choose the heavier one." The hard limit now reads "level 3 by default, level 4 only for the large spec-driven builds described in level 4". The same wording is in the `sc-recommend` skill, its reference file, their plugin copies, and the `/sc:recommend` CLI prompt; the skill's tie rule no longer lets a level-4 row win a tie against a level-3 row.
+- New rule in the guide and core `CLAUDE.md`: never choose `/task-builder` or `/task` as the planner on your own; use them only when the user names the command or confirms after being told the cost. Skills and commands that run them as one of their own steps (for example `/tech-research`, `/prd`, `/tdd`, `/roadmap`) are exempt.
+- Guide sections 2, 3.1 step 1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4, 3.6, 3.7, 3.8 and 3.11 and the routing rows `simple-plan`, `task-file`, `feature-existing` (now level 3, no `--spec` flag), `research-first`, `shape-idea` and `bug` now send planned work to `/sc:workflow`. The stand-alone task-file walk-through moved to the new section 3.13. The level 6 route (`/prd`, `/tdd`, `/roadmap`) is unchanged.
+- Corrected descriptions: `/sc:troubleshoot --fix` and `/sc:auggie-review` offer a `/sc:workflow` plan by default (a task file only with `--depth deep`); the guide said they offered a task file.
+- `docs/user-guide/commands.md` and `docs/user-guide/session-management.md` match the new levels.
+- New regression tests in `tests/core/test_how_we_work_routing_table.py` fail if the old tie-break or hard-limit wording returns anywhere under `src/` or `plugins/`, or if level 4 again lists "many files" or "more than one session" as a trigger.
+
 ### pr-submit — default monitor level 3; every PR instruction uses `--monitor 3`
 
